Jorge Llambias wrote:


>   do catlu be le nu mi klama
> 
> could parse as: do (catlu be le nu mi) klama

No, that is impossible.  NU has to be followed by a bridi,
which must include a selbri.

> or as: do catlu be le nu (mi klama)

That's the only possible parse.  To express the meaning of the
first case would require:

	do catlu be le nu mi co'e cu klama

where cu could be replaced by be'o or kei.
